{%- comment %} Ported from /home/rmdes/zachleat.com/static/defer.js.liquid.
Source dropped this file at project root (dir.input = "."), so its
`{% include "../node_modules/..." %}` resolved one level up, straight into
node_modules. This theme's dir.input is "content" (eleventy.config.js), and
Eleventy only template-processes files under dir.input — a `static/` dir at
the project root (where the passthrough-only "static/js/*" assets already
live, see eleventyConfig.addPassthroughCopy({ static: "/" })) would just be
copied verbatim as an unprocessed ".liquid" file, front matter and all,
never landing at /static/defer.js. Placed under content/static/ instead —
the same pattern this theme already uses for content/_css/ to reach a
top-level output path — so Liquid's engine actually renders it. That adds
one extra directory of depth versus the source, so the include climbs two
levels (content/static/ -> content/ -> project root) instead of one.

Source also concatenates two @zachleat/* npm widgets (filter-container,
fundraising-status) after is-land.js — neither is a dependency of this
theme (package.json has no reference to either), and nothing here uses
<filter-container> or fundraising-status markup, so only the island loader
is ported. {% endcomment -%}
